 "name": "BPW85B",
 "kind": "sensor",
 "manufacturer": "Vishay Semiconductors",
 "title": "BPW85, BPW85A, BPW85B, BPW85C: silicon NPN phototransistor in a clear 3 mm (T-1) leaded package",
 "source": {
  "document": "Document Number 81531",
  "revision": "Rev. 2.1, 04-Aug-14",
  "pages": 6
 },
 "summary": "A two-lead silicon NPN phototransistor, collector and emitter only, in a clear 3 mm (T-1) plastic package, sensitive to visible and near-infrared radiation. Its spectral bandwidth at 10 % runs from 450 nm to 1080 nm with the peak at 850 nm, and its half-sensitivity angle is ±25°. The four part numbers are sorts by collector light current at 1 mW/cm² and 950 nm: BPW85 covers 0.8 to 8 mA, BPW85A 0.8 to 2.5 mA, BPW85B 1.5 to 4 mA and BPW85C 3 to 8 mA. Its named use is as a detector in control and drive electronics.",
